### 4.9 Historical Backcasting Validation

Before any forward projection is reported, the model is run from 2010 to 2020 with AI parameters at their 2010 values (near zero) and τ_EMP^(cross-border) at pre-pandemic values (approximately 0.10). The model must replicate:

(a) Net growth in global migration stock from 222M (2010) to 281M (2020);
(b) Directional patterns of post-2008 European migration shifts, specifically Eastern European outflow to Germany and UK;
(c) Relative stability of bilateral wage ratios in the 40 primary corridors in the absence of AI augmentation.

Failure to replicate any of these three stylized facts within ±15% constitutes a model specification failure requiring recalibration before forward simulation is reported. This criterion is stated here, prior to running the model, to prevent post-hoc specification search.

